WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.720
With Avengers: Infinity War, the Marvel Cinematic
Universe is heading towards a conflict that's

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.020
been building for nearly a decade.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.429
Thanos has been on a collision course with
the rest of the heroes since 2012's Avengers,

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:14.179
and he's finally taking center stage in a
battle for the Infinity Stones.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:19.430
The war will unite an entire universe of superheroes,
but it'll also likely have lethal consequences.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.730
Given the stakes involved and the Mad Titan's
status as the ultimate bad guy of the Marvel

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.750
movies, the question isn't if one of the heroes
won't make it out alive, but which one.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.100
"I hope they remember you."

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.660
Let's take a look at the cast of Infinity
War to come up with our best betting odds

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.280
on which heroes might not make it to the closing
credits.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.170
Watch out for potential spoilers as we figure
out who's going to meet their maker… and

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.380
we don't mean Stan lee.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.960
"Are you Tony Stank?"

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.000
Black Panther

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.899
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has doled out
more than its share of jaw-dropping surprises

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:55.239
over the last decade, and the studio's braintrust
has proven itself more than willing to take

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:57.949
bold creative risks with the franchise's storytelling.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:02.460
But Marvel Studios also has to consider its
bottom line, and since Black Panther just

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.130
became one of the highest-grossing superhero
movies of all time, there's no way the executives

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.900
are going to let him get away that easily.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.880
Forget about his Vibranium stockpile, pulling
in that much money at the theater is what

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.590
really makes T'Challa bulletproof.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.440
There's just no way Wakanda's king isn't one
of the heroes left standing once Infinity

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.540
War is over.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.260
Odds: 1.239 billion (and counting) to 1

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.600
Spider-Man

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.390
Also far too promising for dismantlement right
now is Spider-Man.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.460
Granted, Peter Parker is going to be completely
outmatched against Thanos and seems to be

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.100
primed to suffer some serious punishment in
the movie.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.880
But with a second Spider-Man: Homecoming movie
due in theaters next year, the chances of

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.540
him being truly taken out by Thanos seem slim.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.800
He's just way too new and too popular to meet
his end just yet.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.240
"You're that spider guy on YouTube, right?"

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.160
"Call me Spider-Man!"

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.960
"Okay, Spider-Man! Do a Flip!"

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.160
"Yeaaaahh!"

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.640
Odds: 100 to 1

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.940
Gamora

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.080
She's the deadliest woman in the galaxy, and
she's got a major grudge against Thanos, who

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.360
basically stole her from her home planet and
tortured her adopted sister.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.310
Gamora might have been Thanos' favorite daughter
growing up, but she doesn't seem to have much

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.810
love for the Mad Titan now.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.450
It seems more likely that she'd be the one
to take down Thanos than that he'd ever get

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.090
to lay his purple hands on her.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.350
After all, she learned from him.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.500
Odds: 75 to 1

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.000
Black Widow

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.130
Fans have been clamoring for Black Widow to
get a solo movie since she first kicked her

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:27.170
way onto the screen in Iron Man 2, so getting
rid of her before we actually get to see her

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.700
stand alone seems like a catastrophically
bad idea.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.750
That said, Natasha Romanoff's fate during
the Infinity War Saga could go either way.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.450
If it's her backstory that people really want
to see, it doesn't matter much that she survives

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.880
in the current timeline, right?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.220
With Hulk, Captain America, and the Black
Panther at her side, though, she's probably

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.350
still got a good shot of hanging in there
this time.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.880
Odds: 50 to 1

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.280
Hulk

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.200
On one level, Hulk is arguably the easiest
character to get rid of in Infinity War.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.460
He hasn't had a solo movie since 2008's Incredible
Hulk, and he's kind of a liability for the

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.460
Avengers anyway.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.851
With Marvel seeming pretty uninterested in
giving the Hulk a solo spotlight, there's

00:03:01.851 --> 00:03:05.710
a strong possibility that his part in the
franchise might be coming to an end.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.410
It's also worth noting that Mark Ruffalo revealed
that the plan has been to give the Hulk an

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:13.570
arc that would begin in Thor: Ragnarok and
continue through the two Infinity War movies.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.740
In Ragnarok, Bruce became the Hulk for years
at a time, which allowed the Green Guy to

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.630
run the show without Banner's knowledge or
approval.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.560
It's easy to see how that loss of control
might not work out so well for him, then,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:24.440
isn't it?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.660
Odds: 20 to 1

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.160
Thor

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:31.300
Thor: Ragnarok was funny, but it also put
Thor through the wringer.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.150
His hammer was shattered, he lost an eye,
and his homeland of Asgard was destroyed,

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.000
leaving him exiled in outer space.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.970
If the plan is for things to keep getting
worse for the Odinson, then there's really

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.970
not a whole lot left do with him but plant
him under a tombstone.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.750
But with so much coming down on him in his
own movie, Thor seems to be gaining strength.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.040
He's now able to channel his supernatural
gifts, and he's expected to get a new hammer

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.320
in Infinity War, called the Stormbreaker.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.370
So, it seems just as likely that the God of
Thunder's luck will turn around in the film

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.980
as it does that he'll keep getting trounced
by baddies.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.820
Or himself.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.820
"Cuz that's what..."

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.780
Odds: 15 to 1

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.790
Drax

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.980
Of all the Guardians of the Galaxy, Drax seems
like he might be the most likely choice for

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:14.980
the chopping block.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.600
In the comics, his entire reason for living
is to execute Thanos.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.120
Since the movie version tends to launch himself
into battle without thinking of any consequences,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.780
his fast fury could lead to a toe-to-toe fight
with the deadliest being the Marvel Universe

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.780
has to offer.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.550
If that is in fact what happens, it's pretty
hard to imagine Drax coming out as the winner.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.940
At the same time, Dave Bautista's performance
in the Guardians movies have made him a fan

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.940
favorite, so the question is whether the shock
value of having him take one for the team

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.210
is enough to outweigh the benefits of keeping
him around.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.800
Odds: 12 to 1

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.350
Hawkeye

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.250
Even before he was curiously absent from the
film's character-heavy poster, Hawkeye hasn't

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.190
been the most obvious priority for Marvel
Studios, and his arc reflects that.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.060
He's retired, gotten bored enough to join
Captain America's illegal strike force, and

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.230
been imprisoned as a war criminal by Iron
Man.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.930
Those are all pretty good signs that the Marvel
Cinematic Universe doesn't have much left

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:08.840
to do with the archer beyond giving him a
noble death to let everyone else know the

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.690
stakes in the war against Thanos.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:14.410
Let's be real for a second, though: if they
did kill off Hawkeye in Infinity War, would

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.030
you actually even notice?

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.100
Odds: 10 to 1

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.639
Star-Lord

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.540
Another hero who seems unlikely to die at
the hands of the Mad Titan is Peter Quill.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.480
"What the?"

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.700
After all, he's already survived a couple
of cosmic threats before, so what's one more?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.199
Plus, Chris Pratt's comedic chops have set
the tone that the Guardians movies are built

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:38.540
on, and that seems to be carrying through
to Infinity War as well.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.919
"I think it's good, except it sucks.

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:42.490
So, let me do the plan."

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:46.400
On the other hand, Star-Lord's death would
be a huge shock, which might mean it'd be

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.400
worth it just for the sake of keeping audiences
on their toes.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.430
Besides, he's half Living Planet, and as we
all saw in Guardians 2, it takes more than

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:57.040
a couple of blaster bolts to the head to take
one of them out permanently.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.810
Nobody ever said these characters have to
stay dead to make it onto Thanos' kill count

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.889
for this film.

00:06:01.889 --> 00:06:03.870
Odds: 10 to 1

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.590
Doctor Strange

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.760
As the Sorcerer Supreme, Doctor Strange is
the only one who's faced the kind of celestial

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:15.030
threat Thanos represents, taking on Dormammu
by himself and coming away with a victory.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.729
With that kind of win on his record, it seems
likely that Strange's formal introduction

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:21.920
to the Avengers could be the thing that tips
odds in their favor.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.240
"Who's laughing now, a------?"

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:29.840
But his future in the MCU is questionable
at the moment, since even Benedict Cumberbatch

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:33.320
doesn't seem to know whether Doctor Strange
2 is gonna actually happen.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:37.300
The filmmakers did already set up Baron Mordo
as a villain for his next outing, but we'll

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:41.370
have to wait and see whether that pays off,
or if the mystic meets his end in the Infinity

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.370
War instead.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.300
Odds: 8 to 1

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.480
Vision

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.600
He saved the day in Age of Ultron, but since
then, the Vision's had a pretty hard time

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.580
fitting into his role as an Avenger.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.520
In Civil War, he couldn't even stop Hawkeye
and Scarlet Witch from walking out of a room,

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.400
and a misfired laser beam wound up permanently
injuring War Machine, one of his own teammates.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:04.110
With that kind of track record, it's tough
to imagine him lasting long in a fight against

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.110
Thanos.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.270
Moreover, Vision has one of the Infinity Stones
mounted on his forehead, and from the film's

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:13.960
previews, it looks like Thanos' minion Corvus
Glaive might just get to him before it's all

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:14.960
said and done.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.560
Suffice it to say, things aren't looking good
for the Avengers' resident synthezoid.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.720
Odds: 5 to 1

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.460
Nebula

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:27.260
It's no secret that Infinity War is drawing
pretty heavily from the events of 1991's Infinity

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:31.710
Gauntlet storyline, and in that story, Thanos
keeps Nebula suspended just on the verge of

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.340
death as a form of torture to amuse himself.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:38.580
The twist is that Nebula is ultimately able
to get control of the Infinity Stones herself,

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.900
which sets into motion Thanos' defeat.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.250
Since Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 spent
so much time patching up Nebula's relationship

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:49.449
with Gamora — and establishing that Thanos
is no stranger to mutilating her just for

00:07:49.449 --> 00:07:54.110
kicks — having Thanos target his renegade
daughter would be an easy way to show moviegoers

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.550
how ruthless he can be.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:59.130
Or she could end up being one of the people
who helps take him down in the end, as it

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.130
was written.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.130
We'll have to wait and see.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.140
Odds: 5 to 1

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:04.640
Captain America

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:09.460
Steve Rogers is easily the most beloved of
the Avengers, so if the film's producers really

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:13.509
want to hit the audiences with a gut punch,
killing off Captain America would do it.

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:17.410
What better way to reunite the Avengers after
the events of Civil War than having them rally

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.300
around his heroic sacrifice?

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.190
The previews certainly seem to be setting
the tone for a tough fight between Cap and

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.770
Thanos, and Chris Evans himself has confirmed
that he intends to retire from blockbuster

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.020
movies in favor of smaller films.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:33.099
It hardly seems like a coincidence that Steve
Rogers has not one, but two characters that

00:08:33.099 --> 00:08:36.630
could take up his shield if he falls in battle:
Falcon and Bucky Barnes.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.240
Evans has mentioned that he's still set to
appear in the movie that comes after Infinity

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:44.629
War, but there's nothing that says that appearance
won't be in a flashback… or a coffin.

00:08:44.629 --> 00:08:46.670
Odds: 3 to 1

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.680
Iron Man (Tony Stark)

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.329
We don't know for sure, of course, but it
looks like Tony Stark is not going survive

00:08:52.329 --> 00:08:53.329
this movie.

00:08:53.329 --> 00:08:54.329
"Wow."

00:08:54.329 --> 00:08:58.100
It might actually be the only logical conclusion
to a character arc that's been building since

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.399
2008.

00:08:59.399 --> 00:09:03.279
Over the past few movies, Tony's fears about
the changing world, and his efforts to get

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:06.740
ahead of the disasters that come from a world
full of superheroes and villains have gone

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.339
increasingly off the rails.

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:12.550
His attempt to create artificial intelligence
unleashed Ultron and resulted in the complete

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:16.629
destruction of Sokovia, which in turn led
directly to the Avengers themselves being

00:09:16.629 --> 00:09:18.939
destroyed as a team during the events of Civil
War.

00:09:18.939 --> 00:09:23.699
Even his most recent protege, Peter Parker,
was defined by his choice to reject the path

00:09:23.699 --> 00:09:25.209
that Tony took as Iron Man.

00:09:25.209 --> 00:09:29.220
With a conflict that's bigger and more far-reaching
than anything he's dealt with before, the

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:33.440
consequences are going to be just as huge
— and for Tony, that likely means a heroic

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.440
sacrifice.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.679
There's a certain poetry to it.

00:09:35.679 --> 00:09:40.189
Iron Man was the movie that kicked off the
MCU in 2008, and what better way to mark the

00:09:40.189 --> 00:09:43.959
10th anniversary of the cinematic universe
than by killing off its founding character?

00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:47.709
It'd be bittersweet, of course, but it'd be
the best farewell Iron Man could hope for

00:09:47.709 --> 00:09:51.529
to sacrifice himself for the sake of the planet
and the universe at large.

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:53.629
"Tell me his name again."

00:09:53.629 --> 00:09:54.929
Odds: 3 to 2.

00:09:54.929 --> 00:09:56.879
In other words, rest in peace, Iron Man.

00:09:56.879 --> 00:09:58.029
Thanks for watching!

00:09:58.029 --> 00:10:00.839
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:00.839 --> 00:10:03.100
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

